From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Subject: [PATCH] hwcomposer window: report a failed gralloc allocation

HWComposerNativeWindowBuffer's constructor discarded the return value of
hybris_gralloc_allocate(). When the gralloc HAL refuses the allocation (no
memory in the framebuffer heap, a usage or format it does not support) the
buffer is still queued with a NULL handle and the EGL driver then
dereferences the handle: libGLES_mali.so crashed in its render thread on a
SM-T113 (Spreadtrum SC7730S) at handle->format.

Keep the return value as the buffer status, so allocateBuffers() sees the
failure and does not queue the buffer, and print what was asked for and the
error, which is the only place that says why.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 egl/platforms/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_window.cpp | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/egl/platforms/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_window.cpp
+++ b/egl/platforms/hwcomposer/hwcomposer_window.cpp
@@ -106,7 +106,14 @@
     busy = 0;
     status = 0;
 
-    hybris_gralloc_allocate(width, height, format, (uint32_t)usage, &handle, (uint32_t*)&stride);
+    handle = NULL;
+    stride = 0;
+    status = hybris_gralloc_allocate(width, height, format, (uint32_t)usage, &handle, (uint32_t*)&stride);
+    if (status) {
+        fprintf(stderr, "hybris-hwcomposer: gralloc allocate %ux%u format x%x usage x%" PRIx64 " failed: %d (%s)\n",
+                width, height, format, usage, status, strerror(status < 0 ? -status : status));
+        handle = NULL;
+    }
 
     TRACE("width=%d height=%d stride=%d format=x%x usage=x%" PRIx64 "status=%s this=%p",
         width, height, stride, format, usage, strerror(-status), this);
